# Machine-local signing configuration, sourced by scripts/package-app.sh and
# scripts/install.sh when present. Copy to scripts/local.env (gitignored).
#
# Each build lane has its own namespace. Do not use the former unprefixed
# CODESIGN_IDENTITY, INSTALLER_IDENTITY, or PROVISIONING_PROFILE variables:
# sharing those values allowed an App Store distribution profile to be used by
# a direct-install build.

# Debug development lane: scripts/dev.sh / package-app.sh --debug
# Bundle identifier: dev.onetimesecret.pad
#
# DEV_CODESIGN_IDENTITY="Apple Development: Name (TEAMID)"
# DEV_PROVISIONING_PROFILE="$HOME/Library/OnetimePad_Dev.provisionprofile"

# Local dogfood lane: scripts/install.sh / package-app.sh
# Bundle identifier: com.onetimesecret.pad
# Use a macOS development certificate and a macOS development provisioning
# profile authorizing that certificate, this Mac, and this bundle identifier.
# A wildcard TEAMID.* development profile may cover both local lanes.
#
# LOCAL_CODESIGN_IDENTITY="Apple Development: Name (TEAMID)"
# LOCAL_PROVISIONING_PROFILE="$HOME/Library/OnetimePad_Local.provisionprofile"

# App Store/TestFlight lane: package-app.sh --app-store
# Bundle identifier: com.onetimesecret.pad
# Use the exact identity names reported by `security find-identity` and an
# explicit Mac App Store distribution profile for com.onetimesecret.pad.
#
# APP_STORE_CODESIGN_IDENTITY="3rd Party Mac Developer Application: Name (TEAMID)"
# APP_STORE_INSTALLER_IDENTITY="3rd Party Mac Developer Installer: Name (TEAMID)"
# APP_STORE_PROVISIONING_PROFILE="$HOME/Library/OnetimePad_App_Store.provisionprofile"

# Optional App Store build-number counter. The default is
# onetimepad-app-store-build-number in the git common directory, shared by every
# worktree of the clone. This is required outside a git checkout.
#
# APP_STORE_BUILD_NUMBER_FILE="$HOME/Library/OnetimePad-app-store-build-number"

# Provisioning profiles are required only when the lane carries
# scripts/Companion.entitlements. Without a profile, a configured dev/local
# identity still signs the app but the script omits those restricted
# entitlements. To create a development profile at developer.apple.com:
#
#   1. Register explicit macOS App IDs for the lane bundle identifiers, or use a
#      wildcard macOS App ID when the required capabilities permit it.
#   2. Register this Mac's Provisioning UDID (About This Mac, System Report,
#      Hardware, Provisioning UDID).
#   3. Create a macOS App Development profile for the App ID, development
#      certificate, and this Mac.
#   4. Download the profile outside the checkout and set the matching variable.
#
# Before compiling or replacing a bundle, package-app.sh verifies the selected
# profile's team, App ID, Keychain group, certificate, expiry, and profile
# class. On the dev and local lanes it also checks the current Mac's
# Provisioning UDID.
